# Dockerfile.test-runner (testing_mcp/infra/Dockerfile.test-runner)
# Template for the "ship .git HEAD so the exact-HEAD guard runs in Cloud Run" fix.
#
# The current Dockerfile installs `git` (line 12) but never COPYs the .git/ tree,
# so the `_configure_exact_head_python_runtime()` guard at test_level_up_organic.py:5348
# crashes on `git rev-parse HEAD` with "fatal: not a git repository".
#
# Apply this template by adding the two COPY lines (marked # <-- ADD) AFTER the
# `COPY --chown=appuser:appuser testing_mcp/ ./testing_mcp/` block, and the
# GIT_COMMIT env-var fallback in the entrypoint.
#
# Verified pattern: 2026-08-13 investigation on the wa-daily-level-up-test-mr6dk run.

# --- existing block (for context) ---
# COPY --chown=appuser:appuser testing_mcp/ ./testing_mcp/
# COPY --chown=appuser:appuser mvp_site/ ./mvp_site/
# COPY --chown=appuser:appuser testing_utils/ ./testing_utils/
# COPY --chown=appuser:appuser infrastructure/ ./infrastructure/
# COPY --chown=appuser:appuser testing_mcp/infra/entrypoint.sh ./entrypoint.sh

# --- add these two lines (cheapest fix: only HEAD + ref, not full .git) ---
# COPY --chown=appuser:appuser .git/HEAD ./.git/HEAD
# COPY --chown=appuser:appuser .git/refs/heads/ ./.git/refs/heads/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Alternative (preferred when build-time GIT_COMMIT is known): pass as build-arg
# and write a synthetic .git/HEAD + .git/refs/heads/main in the build step.
#
# ARG GIT_COMMIT
# RUN if [ -n "$GIT_COMMIT" ]; then \
#       mkdir -p ./.git/refs/heads/main && \
#       echo "ref: refs/heads/main" > ./.git/HEAD && \
#       echo "$GIT_COMMIT" > ./.git/refs/heads/main/COMMIT_SHA && \
#       chown -R appuser:appuser ./.git; \
#     fi
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Pair this with the entrypoint fallback (see template: entrypoint-git-fallback.sh)
# so that if a future Dockerfile change accidentally drops the COPY, the test still
# runs (with a stderr warning) instead of crashing the whole daily cron.
